(6775238, 1015581, 114225, '<td valign="top">What a cool idea. If you could do this, every farmer in the world would hire you.</td>', 'What a cool idea. If you could do this, every farmer in the world would hire you.', '2012-05-22 10:56:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6775240, 1015659, 114225, '<td valign="top">The best ripple photo I have seen in a long time.</td>', 'The best ripple photo I have seen in a long time.', '2012-05-22 10:57:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6775364, 1015581, 12611, '<td valign="top">whimsical and eye pleasing.</td>', 'whimsical and eye pleasing.', '2012-05-22 14:40:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6775366, 1015866, 12611, '<td valign="top">I love the areas of blur and depth; the beautiful shadows. Staring at that back tree line reveals a clarity that is not apparent when staring at the water in front.</td>', 'I love the areas of blur and depth; the beautiful shadows. Staring at that back tree line reveals a clarity that is not apparent when staring at the water in front.', '2012-05-22 14:42:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6775397, 1016053, 125275, '<td valign="top">This is great and I recognize the profile of Christophe. I definitely see another ribbon here, and my only preference would be to remove the rainbow. Still, nicely done!<br/> <br/>I''m coming back to add...I always admire the detail you put into your works so on that note I thought you would like a mention of a small point about the rainbow. The shadows of the tree and person indicate the source of light is in the same direction in the sky as the rainbow itself and this would not be possible unless this is a "moonbow," as rainbows are in the opposite side of the sky as the sun. I see the "point of view" is that the rainbow appears to be originating from the pipe, but I thought you''d appreciate somebody paying close attention. :) Again, well done and I love the effect. Now, I''ve got to comment on some other photos!</td>', 'This is great and I recognize the profile of Christophe. I definitely see another ribbon here, and my only preference would be to remove the rainbow. Still, nicely done! I''m coming back to add...I always admire the detail you put into your works so on that note I thought you would like a mention of a small point about the rainbow. The shadows of the tree and person indicate the source of light is in the same direction in the sky as the rainbow itself and this would not be possible unless this is a "moonbow," as rainbows are in the opposite side of the sky as the sun. I see the "point of view" is that the rainbow appears to be originating from the pipe, but I thought you''d appreciate somebody paying close attention. :) Again, well done and I love the effect. Now, I''ve got to comment on some other photos!', '2012-05-22 15:34:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6775398, 1015270, 125275, '<td valign="top">I love this and it''s perfect. One of my top rated and it''s an interesting choice to use a "portrait" orientation. I highly approve!<br/> <br/>I have a feeling I know who shot this, but I''m holding off on mentioning my guess. I will let you know! :-D</td>', 'I love this and it''s perfect. One of my top rated and it''s an interesting choice to use a "portrait" orientation. I highly approve! I have a feeling I know who shot this, but I''m holding off on mentioning my guess. I will let you know! :-D', '2012-05-22 15:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
