(6777858, 1015043, 54446, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> Before you thought of spring,<br/>Except as a surmise,<br/>You see, God bless his suddenness,<br/>A fellow in the skies<br/>Of independent hues,<br/>A little weather-worn,<br/>Inspiriting habiliments<br/>Of indigo and brown.<br/>With specimens of song,<br/>As if for you to choose,<br/>Discretion in the interval,<br/>With gay delays he goes<br/>To some superior tree<br/>Without a single leaf,<br/>And shouts for joy to nobody<br/>But his seraphic self! </i></td></tr></table> <br/><a href="//www.inspirationalstories.com/poems/before-you-thought-of-spring-emily-dickinson-poem/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Another lovely Emily Dickinson poem</a>.  Thanks very much!</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Before you thought of spring,Except as a surmise,You see, God bless his suddenness,A fellow in the skiesOf independent hues,A little weather-worn,Inspiriting habilimentsOf indigo and brown.With specimens of song,As if for you to choose,Discretion in the interval,With gay delays he goesTo some superior treeWithout a single leaf,And shouts for joy to nobodyBut his seraphic self!  Another lovely Emily Dickinson poem.  Thanks very much!', '2012-05-25 01:05:20.000000', NULL, 0);
