(6778058, 1015581, 119012, '<td valign="top">glad to see this ribbon, it was my only 10. even though the cloud itself looked a tad fake, the creativity and execution behind this shot outweighed that minor flaw.<br/> <br/>well done!</td>', 'glad to see this ribbon, it was my only 10. even though the cloud itself looked a tad fake, the creativity and execution behind this shot outweighed that minor flaw. well done!', '2012-05-25 06:58:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778066, 1016018, 142363, '<td valign="top">Brilliant - one of my three 10''s for this challenge - and thank you for explaining how you did it.  I was wondering about that!  It''s an absolutely stunning submission!</td>', 'Brilliant - one of my three 10''s for this challenge - and thank you for explaining how you did it.  I was wondering about that!  It''s an absolutely stunning submission!', '2012-05-25 07:37:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778067, 1016018, 92577, '<td valign="top">Hope you don''t mind me saying I''m more impressed by this than by the peacock! - Shared my top vote.</td>', 'Hope you don''t mind me saying I''m more impressed by this than by the peacock! - Shared my top vote.', '2012-05-25 07:39:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778080, 1016075, 103032, '<td valign="top">Thought I''d comment here instead of <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1149128&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">your thread.</a>  I gave this an 8 (the highest score I gave in this challenge.)  I liked the image and your processing.  I felt it fit the challenge, felt like it represented "in the rain."  The blur works well in this image in that it left me to imagine what was going on, it allows me to develop a story for the image.  This compared to Blue Monday, I probably would have scored Blue Monday higher because I would have associated the blue tone with cold, as is the rain...  Overall, this is a great image. <br/> <br/>Personally, I don''t judge an image based on if it was processed to the fullest extent of the rule set (expert editing).  I vote on how it resonates with me...<br/> <br/>Images resonate with some people, they don''t with others.  In the bell curve, more people liked this image than those that didn''t like it so much... So it''s a winner :)</td>', 'Thought I''d comment here instead of your thread.  I gave this an 8 (the highest score I gave in this challenge.)  I liked the image and your processing.  I felt it fit the challenge, felt like it represented "in the rain."  The blur works well in this image in that it left me to imagine what was going on, it allows me to develop a story for the image.  This compared to Blue Monday, I probably would have scored Blue Monday higher because I would have associated the blue tone with cold, as is the rain...  Overall, this is a great image.  Personally, I don''t judge an image based on if it was processed to the fullest extent of the rule set (expert editing).  I vote on how it resonates with me... Images resonate with some people, they don''t with others.  In the bell curve, more people liked this image than those that didn''t like it so much... So it''s a winner :)', '2012-05-25 07:57:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778086, 1016069, 20799, '<td valign="top">In my voting list you were beaten only by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=11769" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jmritz</a>''s butt shot - sorry :). Awesome image, perfect counterpointing. I like how the reflection crosses over to the <strike>shadow</strike> arrow, for me that is the strongest part of the composition, adding a breaking point and making you wonder.<br/>I''ve read about the color shift, don''t know about that but colors look just fabulous. Cestitam! :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-05-26 16:52:24.</i></td>', 'In my voting list you were beaten only by  jmritz''s butt shot - sorry :). Awesome image, perfect counterpointing. I like how the reflection crosses over to the shadow arrow, for me that is the strongest part of the composition, adding a breaking point and making you wonder.I''ve read about the color shift, don''t know about that but colors look just fabulous. Cestitam! :-)', '2012-05-25 08:18:14.000000', '2012-05-26 17:52:24.000000', 0),
(6778087, 1016018, 129807, '<td valign="top">Ha! Just came back for another look at this and tried to add it to my Favourites. I received an ERROR - I''d already added it. :o)<br/>Still love this, obviously.</td>', 'Ha! Just came back for another look at this and tried to add it to my Favourites. I received an ERROR - I''d already added it. :o)Still love this, obviously.', '2012-05-25 08:24:23.000000', NULL, 0),
