(6778248, 1015581, 96751, '<td valign="top">Love this. Awesome combination of fantasy/reality.  Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Love this. Awesome combination of fantasy/reality.  Congrats on the ribbon.', '2012-05-25 12:27:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778250, 1016053, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mlianopr:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> It''s a beautiful image, but it''s not photographic in nature.  By that, I mean one would never see this with one''s eyes.  It''s a joy to view, but it''s pure fantasy.  Since this is an expert edit challenge, I will mark this 10, but I don''t accept it as a photograph.  Really enjoy your ability to draw and paint.  No offense intended. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Was thinking almost the same!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m not sure to understand your reasoning. You''re of course free to think what you want, but with all respect due, many photos (even achieved with no or minimal editing) are nothing that could be seen with one''s eyes directly (lens baby, B&amp;W, wide angle, fisheye, long exposure, etc.). Consequently, I don''t believe that if a scene can''t be seen as such with one''s eyes, then it automatically isn''t photography. I also don''t believe photography can only depict hard cold reality, many other uses are possible. IMHO, of course.</td>', 'Originally posted by mlianopr: Originally posted by hahn23: It''s a beautiful image, but it''s not photographic in nature.  By that, I mean one would never see this with one''s eyes.  It''s a joy to view, but it''s pure fantasy.  Since this is an expert edit challenge, I will mark this 10, but I don''t accept it as a photograph.  Really enjoy your ability to draw and paint.  No offense intended.   Was thinking almost the same!!   I''m not sure to understand your reasoning. You''re of course free to think what you want, but with all respect due, many photos (even achieved with no or minimal editing) are nothing that could be seen with one''s eyes directly (lens baby, B&W, wide angle, fisheye, long exposure, etc.). Consequently, I don''t believe that if a scene can''t be seen as such with one''s eyes, then it automatically isn''t photography. I also don''t believe photography can only depict hard cold reality, many other uses are possible. IMHO, of course.', '2012-05-25 12:28:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6778253, 1015878, 12611, '<td valign="top">I enjoyed this a great deal. The overall lightness of the overcast day works with the rain as sort of a sun shower. My only thought is that the dunes in the mid- to upper left of the shot add balance, but may steal thunder away from the scope and perspective of the fisherman.</td>', 'I enjoyed this a great deal. The overall lightness of the overcast day works with the rain as sort of a sun shower. My only thought is that the dunes in the mid- to upper left of the shot add balance, but may steal thunder away from the scope and perspective of the fisherman.', '2012-05-25 12:36:26.000000', NULL, 0),
